        {
          "id": "u5l2",
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Il, lo, la, i, gli, le",
          "dictionaryRefs": [
            "il-libro",
            "lo-studente",
            "la-casa",
            "amico",
            "lo-zaino",
            "la-scuola"
          ],
          "grammarNotes": "GLI ARTICOLI DETERMINATIVI — the definite article ('the') has six forms:\n\nMASCULINE singular:\n• il — before a regular consonant: il libro, il bar\n• lo — before s+consonant, z, gn, ps, x, y: lo studente, lo zaino, lo gnocco, lo psicologo, lo yogurt\n• l' — before a vowel: l'amico, l'anno\n\nMASCULINE plural:\n• i — for 'il' words: il libro → i libri\n• gli — for 'lo' and 'l'' words: lo studente → gli studenti, lo zaino → gli zaini, l'amico → gli amici\n\nFEMININE singular:\n• la — before a consonant: la casa, la scuola (feminine does NOT change before s+consonant!)\n• l' — before a vowel: l'amica, l'età\n\nFEMININE plural (always one form):\n• le — la casa → le case, l'amica → le amiche\n\nWHY lo/gli? Clusters like s+consonant, z, gn, ps are hard to pronounce after 'il' — 'il studente' trips the tongue. Italian smooths them with 'lo'. Same reason English says 'an apple', not 'a apple'.\n\nWHY l'? Two vowels in a row (la amico) are clumsy, so the article drops its vowel: l'amico.\n\nNOTE: Italian uses 'the' much more than English. English says 'Books are expensive'; Italian says 'I libri sono cari' — with the article.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "u5l2e1",
              "type": "fill_blank",
              "prompt": "Choose the article. (The student arrives.)",
              "sentence": "___ studente arriva.",
              "answers": [
                "Lo"
              ],
              "explanation": "'Studente' starts with s+consonant → 'lo'. 'Il studente' would be hard to say, so Italian uses the smoother 'lo'.",
              "dictionaryRefs": [
                "lo-studente"
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "u5l2e2",
              "type": "fill_blank",
              "prompt": "Choose the article. (The friends arrive.)",
