        {
          "id": "u8l2",
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Chi, che, dove, quando, perché, come, quanto",
          "dictionaryRefs": [
            "chi",
            "quando",
            "perche",
            "quanto",
            "lavorare",
            "studiare"
          ],
          "grammarNotes": "LE DOMANDE — asking questions.\n\nTHE QUESTION WORDS:\n• chi — who: 'Chi è?' (Who is it?)\n• che / cosa — what: 'Che fai?' / 'Cosa fai?' (What are you doing? — both correct, cosa is more common)\n• dove — where: 'Dove abiti?'\n• quando — when: 'Quando vieni?'\n• perché — why (AND because): 'Perché studi italiano?' — 'Perché è bello.'\n• come — how: 'Come ti chiami?' (Unit 1)\n• quanto — how much/many: 'Quanto costa?'\n\nTWO RULES ONLY:\n1. The question word comes FIRST, then the normal sentence: 'Dove lavori?' = Where + you-work. No inversion, no 'do' — nothing like English 'Where DO you work?'\n2. Without a question word, just raise your voice (Unit 2): 'Lavori qui?'\n\nQUANTO AGREES (light touch): quanto costa? (m sing), quanta gente (f sing), quanti anni (m pl — you know 'Quanti anni hai?'), quante lettere (f pl). For now: quanti + masculine plural, quante + feminine plural.\n\nPERCHÉ doubles as 'because': question and answer use the same word.",
          "exercises": [
            {
              "id": "u8l2e1",
              "type": "fill_blank",
              "prompt": "Complete the question. (___ are you coming to the bar? — At eight.)",
