            "acqua",
            "vorrei",
            "per-favore"
          ],
          "grammarNotes": "GLI ARTICOLI INDETERMINATIVI — 'a/an' in Italian:\n\n• un — masculine, regular: un caffè, un cornetto, un libro\n• uno — masculine, s+consonant / z / gn / ps: uno studente, uno zaino (same rule as 'lo', Unit 5!)\n• una — feminine, consonant: una scuola, una casa\n• un' — feminine, vowel: un'acqua, un'amica\n\nWHY: the same sound-smoothing as il/lo/la. 'Un studente' trips the tongue → 'uno studente'. 'Una acqua' doubles the vowel → 'un'acqua'.\n\nORDERING POLITELY — set phrases (learn them whole; the grammar of 'vuoi'/'vorrei' comes much later):\n• 'Vorrei un caffè.' — I would like a coffee. (polite)\n• 'Vuoi un caffè?' — Do you want a coffee? (friendly — the invitation)\n• 'Per me un cornetto.' — For me, a croissant.\n• 'Il conto, per favore.' — The bill, please.\n\nCULTURE NOTE: in Italy a 'bar' is a café. 'Un caffè' = an espresso. Cappuccino is a MORNING drink — ordering one after lunch marks you as a tourist. And locals often drink standing at the counter ('al banco'): fast, cheap, social.",
